{"author":{"id":"89da5fec8eff6d69dbcdd68f81be7e9163b16f34b17e978ecf3554487379f453"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1774044534,"nonce":"Q6SCAWubXB5nycuxRoF7cpHqx1g=","title":"Mandible MCP channel server — universal agent integration layer","message":"Build an MCP server that exposes Mandible's event system as a Claude Code channel. Any Claude session running with --channels server:mandible gets real-time Mandible integration.\n\n## Architecture\n\nThe channel server is a thin MCP adapter over Mandible's existing HTTP API (similar pattern to HumbleB's server.py which forwards MCP requests to an HTTP backend).\n\n**Tools (agent → Mandible):**\n- check_inbox — returns pending continuations, auth results, work units\n- report_work_status — agent reports progress/completion\n- submit_auth_request — submit auth requests from within the session\n- get_open_issues — list available work\n- request_work — pull-based work-unit assignment\n\n**Notifications (Mandible → agent):**\n- inbox_item — new continuation, auth result, or work-unit assignment\n- auth_resolved — auth request approved/rejected/completed\n- work_unit_assigned — work dispatched to this session\n- build_completed — daemon rebuild completed\n\n**Instructions:** Teach Claude how to handle Mandible events, when to check inbox, how to report status.\n\n## Why this matters\n\nThis is the distribution story for end users:\n1. User installs Mandible (local daemon)\n2. User already has Claude Code installed with their claude.ai login\n3. User runs: claude --channels server:mandible\n4. Full Mandible integration — no API keys, no OAuth, no auth configuration\n\nMandible never touches the user's auth. It's pure local infrastructure. The user's Claude Code handles all authentication. This completely sidesteps the ToS concern about OAuth-mediated API access.\n\nThis also makes external CLI support first-class — channel-connected sessions get the same integration quality as SDK sessions (minus permission delegation and abort).\n\n## Blockers\n- Channels are in research preview (allowlist, --dangerously-load-development-channels for custom servers)\n- claude.ai login required (fine for our use case — users use their own Claude Code)\n- MCP channel protocol may change before GA\n\n## Implementation\n- New package/directory in Mandible repo for the MCP server\n- stdio transport (Claude Code spawns it as a subprocess)\n- Polls/SSE-subscribes to Mandible HTTP API for event sourcing\n- Stateless — all state lives in Mandible daemon\n\nSee umbrella issue f3dbb3e for the broader inbox/work-unit context.","files":null}]}